HealthCheck.sh

This is a lightweight, dependency free Bash script for auditing a single Linux
host's health and firewall activity, with results pushed to Slack,
Microsoft Teams, and/or email. Built for hosts (bastions, gateways,
small-shop servers) where a full monitoring stack (Nagios, Zabbix,
Prometheus) would be overkill.

This is a work in progress.

What it checks

-Root partition disk usage           -> df -h
-Reachability of a host list         -> ping -c 1
-Firewall log activity (REJECT/DROP/ERROR) -> grep across /var/log/*
-Active firewall ruleset             -> iptables -L, nft list ruleset,
                                          firewall-cmd --list-all-zones
-Open listening ports                -> ss -lntu
-System resource stats               -> vmstat -w


Notifications

connector() is a routes to one or more of three
channels based on a single argument:
 
   1        -> Microsoft Teams
   2        -> Slack
   3        -> Email
   12/13/23/123 -> any combination of the above
 
-teamsConnector: intended to POST an Adaptive Card to a Teams
  incoming webhook. NOT YET DONE
-slackConnector: intended to POST to a Slack incoming webhook.
-sendEmail: pipes a result file into sendmail.

Usage

./HealthCheck.sh <notify_option> <sender_email> <receiver_email>

Example  notify via Slack and email:

./HealthCheck.sh 23 healthcheck@example.com oncall@example.com

Setup

-Place an `ip.txt` file (one hostname/IP per line) in the directory
  the script is run from.
-The invoking user needs sudo to: mkdir, grep on
  /var/log/*, iptables, nft, and firewall-cmd.
-sendmail must be installed and configured on the host for email
  notifications to work.
-A Slack incoming webhook URL is required for Slack notifications.

Security Notes

-This script requires sudo for several operations
-Any webhook URL or API secret ever committed to this script (or
 pasted anywhere outside a secrets manager) should be treated as
 compromised and rotated.

